    "explanation": "To both parties: this dispute is about what the trip cost, but the policy decides it on how far the car actually went, and on that measurement the claim does not survive.\n\nBoth sides agree on the facts, and the record is clean. The GPS trace for TRP-00537 (EV-GPS-00537, weight 1.0) records 4.59 km against the booked optimal route of 4.5 km (EV-TRIP-00537, weight 1.0) — an excess of 0.09 km, or 2.0% of optimal. POL-RD-01 establishes a route deviation only where the excess is BOTH more than 0.8 km in absolute terms AND more than 20% of optimal. Neither gate is passed, so no deviation is established on this trip and the policy directs NO_ACTION however the trip felt to the rider.\n\nBecause no deviation is established, POL-RD-02's recomputation does not run. The SGD 5.10 refund figure carried inside EV-FARE-00537 is a hypothetical computed only for the case where POL-RD-01 is satisfied, and it is not payable here. The charge that stands is SGD 28.45 (charged_total on EV-FARE-00537): metered base 3.80 + distance 3.45 + time 5.32 = 12.57, uplifted by the 2.2x surge recorded on fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier to 27.654, plus the 0.80 platform fee. The rider's real grievance — noon versus 9 pm — is that surge, and it is a lawful part of the metered fare model; the policy reads the multiplier from the fare_breakdown and no clause refunds it, and the driver's statement that surge was showing at booking is consistent with the ledger.\n\nOn billing integrity, EV-FARE-00537 itemises no ERP or toll lines (total 0.00, erp_gantries empty) and no airport surcharge (0.00), so POL-RD-09(4) has nothing to correct and no referral arises. On trace integrity, EV-GPS-00537 is not impaired under POL-RD-07(a)–(c): 115 fixes at a 10 s cadence, 100% coverage, empty gaps, 0 s maximum gap. No corroboration question therefore arises, and no exculpatory clause is needed. The chat log EV-CHAT-00537 is empty and no pickup or dropoff amendment appears, so POL-RD-04 and POL-RD-05 are unavailable; and no driver compensation is due, because the rider was billed 4.6 km against a 4.59 km trace — there is no unbilled distance.\n\nThe traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00537-01 is absent (status MISSING, weight_multiplier 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT). Neither party asserted an external traffic cause, so its absence is a gap in the bundle rather than a contradiction, and it triggers no escalation.\n\nResult: NO_ACTION. The fare_breakdown's payment_status remains CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd remains 0.00; the disputed SGD 28.45 is neither refunded nor held. No referral is made, because no clause produces one on these facts.",
